        "heading": "Why Brands Migrate to Shopify Plus",
        "sub_heading": "Most eCommerce platforms don’t scale well. They slow you down, cost more to maintain, and make even simple changes feel like a dev sprint.",
        "text": "<p>Here’s what brands are leaving behind:</p><ul><li><strong>Magento</strong>: Endless updates, hosting headaches, and dev reliance.</li><li><strong>WooCommerce</strong>: Plugin conflicts, fragile themes, inconsistent checkout.</li><li><strong>Salesforce</strong>: High licensing costs, complex workflows, and vendor lock-in.</li><li><strong>BigCommerce</strong>: Rigid templates, design limits, and dated UX.</li></ul><p>When you <strong>migrate from Salesforce to Shopify Plus</strong>, or any platform for that matter, you're unlocking faster deployment, easier workflows, and lower total cost of ownership.</p>",
